Q1: Does top_postseason_team_scores read precomputed_team_scores.school_id or join by name?\
\
I cannot answer this with certainty. The function does not exist in any file in this repo \'97 it was created directly in the dashboard. I can't call pg_get_functiondef via the PostgREST API (no exec_sql RPC is exposed). You need to run this in the Supabase SQL editor and look at the SELECT list:\
\
SELECT pg_get_functiondef(oid) FROM pg_proc WHERE proname = 'top_postseason_team_scores';\
\
Two things to look for:\
- pts.school_id (or equivalent column read) \uc0\u8594  reads from cache \u8594  patching the table works\
- JOIN schools s ON s.display_name = pts.school_name \uc0\u8594  joins by name \u8594  patching school_id is irrelevant\
\
What I can infer from evidence: The observable behavior \'97 NULL school_ids flowing through the RPC for exactly the schools with NULL in the cache, non-null flowing through for the rest \'97 is consistent with both hypotheses. A name-join on schools.display_name would also return NULL for 'Christian Brothers Academy' (no match to 'Christian Brothers'). I cannot distinguish the two cases from outside the function.\
\
The indirect evidence favors hypothesis A (reads cache column directly): every migration note describing this function says "reads ONLY from precomputed_team_scores" with no mention of an additional join, and the rescue_girls migration fixed logos by re-inserting with correct school_ids \'97 not by changing school_names. But that's circumstantial.\
\
Run that SQL. The logos question lives or dies on what comes back.\
